			"author": {
				"name": "Eric Portis",
				"url": "https://front-end.social/@eeeps",
				"avatarUrl": "https://avatars.webmention.io/cdn.masto.host/6b3b9bc7dd2b1579c5120214de95fac1f65d50c215f38f3253cf8c43cf33a361.jpg"
			},
			"date": "2025-02-28T15:39:57.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> 1) Yellows FTW (C+L champions) 2) What do you use when there is no color that meets your 0.4&lt;x&lt;0.95 filter? 3) Did something go wrong without the concurrency queue that led you to it, or was it a defensive move? I don't have good intuitions about when adding something like that is worth it/not.</p>",
			"type": "reply",
			"via": "webmention"
		},
		{
			"id": 1888273,
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/hejchristian.com/post/3ljasialyec2e",
			"author": {
				"name": "Christian Alder",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/hejchristian.com",
				"avatarUrl": "https://avatars.webmention.io/cdn.bsky.app/b926eb2449e74d457ee802d4c45d70131fa934bc90269fbca096f76793d06176.jpg"
			},
			"date": "2025-02-28T16:15:11.000Z",
			"content": "Yay! I was hoping there might be a blog post when I saw that plugin drop the other day ???? Thanks!",
			"type": "reply",
			"via": "webmention"
		},
		{
			"id": 1888327,
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat/114082557558388698",
			"author": {
				"name": "Zach Leatherman :11ty:",
				"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat",
				"avatarUrl": "https://avatars.webmention.io/cdn.masto.host/14ce4eedb6fa8c93ac6e7e3bb2fe381ed3e096f00f61e664def82c368d89c1d7.png"
			},
			"date": "2025-02-28T16:54:41.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://front-end.social/@eeeps\" class=\"u-url\">@<span>eeeps</span></a></span> I think the default is just a light gray but it definitely happens!</p><p>Yeah, I usually try to add a concurrency queue (and heavier caching) for things that can/might fetch out to remote sources — definitely a defensive move after I saw some build failure flakiness in some deps</p>",
			"type": "reply",
			"via": "webmention"
		},
